      "hints": [
        "Factor out $9$ from $9x^2 - 36x$.",
        "Complete the square on $x^2 - 4x$.",
        "Expand and combine constant terms."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factorise the leading coefficient $9$ from the first two terms:\n$$9x^2 - 36x + 8 = 9(x^2 - 4x) + 8$$",
        "Complete the square inside the bracket:\n$$x^2 - 4x = (x - 2)^2 - 2^2 = (x - 2)^2 - 4$$",
        "Expand and simplify into the required form $p(x + q)^2 + r$:\n$$9[(x - 2)^2 - 4] + 8 = 9(x - 2)^2 - 36 + 8 = 9(x - 2)^2 - 28$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Completing the Square": "Completes the square to obtain $9(x-2)^2 - 28$ with $p=9, q=-2, r=-28$ (B2)."
